{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121747","id":4131028820,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc72On9U","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121747","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121747.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121747.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121747","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121747/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/121747/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121747/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/870efa61543904e621d57c9269f4baaaccf6b0d5","number":121747,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Fix area monitoring logic bugs","user":{"login":"Schnorg","id":44937651,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0OTM3NjUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44937651?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg","html_url":"https://github.com/Schnorg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Schnorg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"- Remove unnecessary BVH shape change triggers from godot_area_2d.cpp\r\n- Consolidate area parameter change logic within godot_area_pair_2d.cpp\r\n- Add fast and simple `has_space_override()` access function to area\r\n- Move `_set_static()` to respond to Monitoring, not Monitorable\r\n- Add virtual functions `refresh_pair(p_source)` to propagate changes via constraint graph\r\n\r\n## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nCloses: #121094\r\nCloses: #100346\r\nCloses: #25331\r\nCloses: #111823\r\nCloses: #81883\r\nCloses: #71489\r\n\r\nCloses for 2D (no MRP to test):\r\n#17238\r\n\r\nMay close or positively impact other issues I haven't fully read or tested, inc:\r\n#14578, #19271, #25769\r\n\r\nSupersedes: #111880\r\n\r\n## What was wrong\r\n\r\nBesides bugs and missing edge cases: \r\n\r\n### Areas were being assigned to the wrong BVH tree\r\nThis PR assigns areas to the static or dynamic BVH tree based on `monitoring` settings, rather than `monitorable`. \r\n\r\nI suspect that `monitorable` was being used because it improved performance in the past, before areas were able to be used dynamically.\r\n\r\nThis fix could have peformance impacts I am happy to discuss, but they seem immaterial in testing of my own games. The peformance impact will be where areas are actually detecting static bodies, in scenarios where they were not before (which was a bug of omission). \r\n\r\n### Parameter changes were propagating via BVH side effects\r\nBasically the code was calling broadphase->move() and sometimes destroying and recreating BVH shapes in the hope that the BVH will then destroy and re-create a constraint pair, which will then check all the collision and monitoring flags anew.\r\n\r\nThis cannot work properly for monitoring/monitorable for complicated reasons. In other cases, the BVH optimizes away the codes attempts to force a constraint re-creation, because it sees that their AABB hasn't changed.\r\n\r\nThis PR consolidates logic for relevant parameter changes within the constraint processing itself. As a result, it should make future fixes and maintenance easier.\r\n\r\n## Testing\r\n\r\nI have tested on MRPs from these issues:\r\n#121094, #100346, #25331, #111823, #81883, #71489, \r\n\r\nI have tested on my own games/prototypes:\r\n*  A side view, physics heavy game with hordes and platform like geometry (inc tilemaps, SmartShapes and polygons). \r\n* A top down shooter with character bodies and areas for collisions.\r\n\r\nI have tested on about 5 other related MRPs and haven't found any regressions. \r\n\r\nMy primary working test was an expanded version of the MRP from #121094. This MRP tests a large number of detection and movement scenarios at once. See below:\r\n\r\n[area-2d.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/30367786/area-2d.zip)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":370471880,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzA0NzE4ODA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:physics","name":"topic:physics","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api